  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the functional representations of our two transformations:\n\n- A reflection across the $y$-axis can be represented by the function \n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(-x,y).\n$$\n\n- Our translation is represented by the function \n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x-7,y-3).\n$$\n\nLet's apply the given transformations to the point $P$ using our functions:\n\nFirst, we apply the reflection. The image of the point $(-6,4)$ under the reflection is\n\n$$\n(-6,4)↦(6,4).\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we apply the translation. The image of the point $(6,4)$ under the translation is\n\n$$\n(6,4)↦(6-7,4-3)=(-1,1).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resulting point is $(-1,1).$",
